%U A398747 2804428024445358986494218681452,2334829601742666973213165311617380699,6498557499332308880358082754249984447155798
%N A398747 Number of 2-dominating sets in the n X n grid graph.
%C A398747 A set S of vertices is 2-dominating if every vertex not in S has at least two neighbors in S (k-domination with k = 2 in the sense of Fink and Jacobson). Members of S carry no requirement.
%C A398747 a(1) = 1 counts the set consisting of the single vertex; the empty set fails because the vertex has no neighbors.
%e A398747 For n = 2, a(2) = 7: every vertex of the 2 X 2 grid has exactly two neighbors, so a vertex outside S needs both of its neighbors in S. The 7 qualifying subsets are the full set, the four 3-subsets, and the two diagonal pairs.
%o A398747 (Python)
%o A398747 from itertools import product
%o A398747 def a(n):
%o A398747     cells = [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(n)]
%o A398747     nb = {c: [(c[0]+d, c[1]+e) for d, e in ((1,0),(-1,0),(0,1),(0,-1)) if 0 <= c[0]+d < n and 0 <= c[1]+e < n] for c in cells}
%o A398747     return sum(all(sum(x in S for x in nb[c]) >= 2 for c in cells if c not in S) for S in ({c for c, b in zip(cells, bits) if b} for bits in product((0, 1), repeat=n*n)))
%Y A398747 Cf. A133515 (dominating sets of the n X n grid), A133793 (total dominating sets), A290382 (minimal dominating sets), A398748 (double total dominating sets).
%K A398747 nonn,more,new
%O A398747 1,2
